# Cursor Rules for PoolAI Project

⚠️ **IMPORTANT**: This file is maintained for backward compatibility.  
**All rules are now in `.cursor/rules/` directory as `.mdc` files.**

## Chat / подальша робота з чатом

При старті сесії або запиті «налаштуйся для роботи з чатом» — **читай `chat-context.mdc`** першим. Там: проект, ключові документи, термінал (MSYS2 only), git (без .sh), патчі, поточний стан і далі.

## Terminal & patches

- **Terminal**: `C:\msys64\usr\bin\bash.exe` (MSYS2 UCRT64) for all local `cargo`/`git`/scripts — no PowerShell, no cmd (see `rust-architect.mdc`, `msys2-windows.mdc`).
- **Patches**: `rust-toolchain.toml`, `.cursor`, `.vscode`, `scripts/`

## Runtime stack

- **`runtime-stack-policy.mdc`** — **alwaysApply:** Rust primary; **zero `.py` in repo**; JS UI; `poolai-openapi-gap-audit` bin.

## Rules Location

All project rules are organized in `.cursor/rules/`:

- **`poolai-agent-roles.mdc`** - 👥 VDT ролі + субагенти + §5.1/§5.12 (always on)
- **`runtime-stack-policy.mdc`** - ⛔ Rust-only runtime; block Python proposals (always on)
- **`chat-context.mdc`** - 🧭 Стартовий контекст чату (при «налаштуйся» / подальша робота)
- **`rust-architect.mdc`** - ⭐ Rust Architect workflow and concept file usage (READ FIRST)
- **`documentation.mdc`** - Documentation structure and file organization rules
- **`git-workflow.mdc`** - Git workflow, commit format, and push order rules
- **`msys2-windows.mdc`** - MSYS2 and Windows development environment rules (bash, NOT PowerShell)
- **`scripts.mdc`** - Scripts structure and file listing rules
- **`project-structure.mdc`** - Project organization and file naming rules
- **`rust.mdc`** - Rust coding standards and patterns
- **`ai-assistant.mdc`** - AI assistant rules and key document references
- **`autonomous-orchestrator.mdc`** - Автономна розробка: оркестратор, субагенти, AUTO_RUN
- **`functionality-management.mdc`** - Менеджер функціоналу: FM-*, охоплення docs, §5.1

## Quick Reference

For detailed rules, see the corresponding file in `.cursor/rules/`:

- Documentation: `.cursor/rules/documentation.mdc`
- Git workflow: `.cursor/rules/git-workflow.mdc`
- MSYS2/Windows: `.cursor/rules/msys2-windows.mdc`
- Scripts: `.cursor/rules/scripts.mdc`
- Project structure: `.cursor/rules/project-structure.mdc`
- Rust patterns: `.cursor/rules/rust.mdc`
- AI assistant: `.cursor/rules/ai-assistant.mdc`
- Chat context: `.cursor/rules/chat-context.mdc`

---

**Note**: Cursor automatically loads rules from `.cursor/rules/` directory.  
This file has been moved to `.cursor/rules/.cursorrules` for better organization.  
All rules are now centralized in `.cursor/rules/` directory.
